{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider does not press a wrong-entrance or wrong-block theory, and POL-NS-03 should not be applied on his behalf: the driver's own trace places him at 24.01 m from the Door 5 pin across 51 consecutive qualifying fixes, roughly 126 m inside the 150 m arrival radius that POL-NS-02 fixes for an AIRPORT pickup, and the pickup pin carries both the label 'Changi Airport Terminal 3, Door 5 ride-hail bay' and venue_id VEN-CHANGI-T3, matching the bay the driver named in the chat log. The rider's general point that the airport is large does not displace that measurement.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09102", "EV-TRIP-09102", "EV-CHAT-09102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Two admissible artifacts contradict each other directly on rider presence in the waiting window and no live clause resolves the conflict, which is the POL-NS-09 escalation condition. The chat log has the rider saying at 22:41:40 'I am walking over now'; the rider track in the GPS artifact records 24 fixes from 22:40:30 to 22:48:10 at a single constant distance of 519.47 m from the pin and a single speed value of 0.0 kph - a device that never moved. POL-NS-04 is the only clause that tests rider position, and it is out of play: limb (b) fails because the driver replied at 22:41:58, 18 seconds after the rider's message, and limb (c) fails on the rider's own track (0 of 24 fixes inside the 200 m AIRPORT rider-presence radius). The rider asks that the fee be held for a human reviewer under POL-NS-09 rather than resolved against him by the automated pipeline; under POL-GEN-03 an escalated amount is held, not collected or refunded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09102", "EV-GPS-09102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's case rests on a 20 second surplus, and the two endpoints of that surplus are the open question a reviewer should settle. The rider does not dispute that the arrival event, the in-geofence fixes, the RIDER_NO_SHOW termination and a continuous run are all present on the face of the record, nor that the single qualifying in-geofence run measures 500 seconds (22:40:00 to 22:48:20) against the 480 second AIRPORT minimum POL-NS-06 sets - a margin of 20 seconds, shortfall -20 s. But the run begins exactly at the trace's first fix and ends exactly at the cancellation second, and the per-fix accuracy values behind the 51 qualifying fixes are not reproduced in the brief. The rider asks the reviewer to verify those two endpoints against the raw trace before the fee is collected.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09102", "EV-TRIP-09102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this pickup road or waiting window: EV-ADVIS-09102-01 is MISSING with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0, and that absence is itself citable under POL-GEN-02. Its effect is that POL-NS-06 limb (i) is unavailable - there is no KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT advisory that could lawfully extend the driver's hold or allow separate in-geofence intervals to be summed - and any attempt by the driver's side to assert limb (i) against this MISSING artifact triggers POL-NS-09 rather than exonerating anyone. Nothing in the record therefore corroborates the driver's run beyond the bare 480 second arithmetic.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09102-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-02", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's profile may not be used to build a finding against him. His prior_no_show_flags (1) and prior_disputes_filed (1), together with his rating and account age, are CONTEXT ONLY under POL-GEN-01, and prior_no_show_flags is a lifetime counter that is not rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d. The rider's citable counters are no_show_disputes_30d, which is 0, and disputes_with_counterparty_90d, which is 0 on both profiles together, so POL-NS-09(c) and POL-NS-09(d) are not engaged and the rider's history cannot be weighed against him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09102", "EV-DPROF-09102"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 4.8,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 4.8,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both parties: this was a genuine rider no-show at Changi T3. The SGD 6.00 cancellation fee is chargeable to the rider, and the driver is paid SGD 4.80 of it. Because the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd (POL-GEN-03): the ruling moves SGD 4.80 to the driver, and the rider's charge of SGD 6.00 stands as it presently is.\n\nFor the driver. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full. (a) The trip record carries an 'arrived' event at 22:40:20. (b) The GPS trace puts the driver about 24 m from the Door 5 pin on 51 consecutive qualifying fixes, well inside the 150 m AIRPORT arrival radius, so arrival is established under POL-NS-02. (c) The driver held position continuously for 500 seconds (22:40:00 to 22:48:20) against the 480-second AIRPORT minimum — a 20-second surplus — measured as the clause requires from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the 'arrived' tap. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 22:48:20 (after the minimum elapsed at 22:48:00) on reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, with no boarding event (started_at and ended_at null). The arrival marker is not false, so POL-NS-05 does not bite: it matches the nearest GPS fix within 20 seconds (limit 90), and at that moment the driver was stationary (0.0 km/h) and 24 m away, nowhere near the 300 m or 15 km/h triggers. POL-NS-03 does not apply, because the driver was inside the arrival radius rather than outside it, so no wrong-entrance or pin-ambiguity goodwill arises. The SGD 6.00 fee reconciles: the greater of the AIRPORT zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_PLUS tier fee (SGD 6.00) is SGD 6.00, matching the fare breakdown, so POL-NS-08(d) raises no integrity defect.\n\nFor the rider. Your non-arrival point is measured and rejected. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate you: the driver replied to 'I am walking over now.' at 22:41:58, 18 seconds after your 22:41:40 message, so limb (b) is not met, and in any event your own track shows 0 of 24 fixes inside the 200 m AIRPORT rider-presence radius. Your escalation request under POL-NS-09 is not made out on any limb. Rider presence is not a fact this ruling turns on — POL-NS-06 refunds or declines whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded — and the chat log and the rider track agree on the material point, that you were not at the bay (about 519 m away, closing in). There is no direct contradiction between admissible artifacts on arrival, dwell or termination: the trace has 51 fixes, no sampling gaps and only 20 seconds of clock skew, all well inside the POL-NS-08(a)–(b) limits, so limb (e) does not fire; both profiles show disputes_with_counterparty_90d of 0 and no_show_disputes_30d of 0, so limbs (c) and (d) do not fire; and the deciding facts are carried by weight-1.0 artifacts, so the POL-GEN-02 confidence cap does not push the case below the 0.70 floor. Your request to verify the 500-second run's endpoints against the raw trace is noted as an open question rather than a ground for escalation: the run is documented by 51 consecutive in-geofence fixes with no gap. The MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09102-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) is citable only for its absence; it makes POL-NS-06 limb (i) unavailable, but that is immaterial, because the dwell cleared the 480-second minimum on its own and there is no shortfall for limb (i) to cure or for you to exploit.\n\nCompensation. With POL-NS-01 satisfied and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of SGD 6.00, that is SGD 4.80, the platform retaining SGD 1.20. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1 divided by 120 completed trips is about 0.008 (below 0.08), so compensation is paid rather than withheld and no escalation follows. No profile field outside those POL-NS-07 names was used against the rider — rating, account age, lifetime counters and prior_no_show_flags are context only under POL-GEN-01, and they were not weighed against you."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
